cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use this software or documentation, please cite the preferred citation below and the source dataset publication."
title: "Cardiac MRI CAD: leakage-controlled, resumable research pipeline"
type: software
authors:
  - family-names: "Marghidan"
    given-names: "David Vlad"
    affiliation: "INFusion Artificial Intelligence Research Laboratory, University of Craiova"
version: "1.0.0"
date-released: "2026-10-05"
license: MIT
keywords:
  - cardiac magnetic resonance
  - coronary artery disease
  - medical image analysis
  - Attention U-Net
  - EfficientNet
  - patient-level validation
  - data leakage
  - shortcut learning
  - reproducibility
abstract: >-
  A patient-level, leakage-controlled research pipeline for a secondary analysis
  of a public cardiac MRI JPEG release. Five cross-fitted 2.5D Attention U-Nets
  produce out-of-fold cardiac masks; frozen EfficientNet-B0 representations compare
  full-image, cardiac-ROI, and complement controls before nested patient-level
  classification. The software is a methodological proof of concept, not a medical device.
